{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Cost Gerrit change 1942 (ticket silken-stealthful-narwhal) a spurious Verified -1: 1 failed, 14508 passed. The failure is unrelated to that change, which touches only scripts/gen_config_reference.py and tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nTEST: tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated\n\nFAILURE (run 32327846364, job 96302879852, ubuntu py3.13, xdist worker gw3):\n\n    shutil.Error: [('.../source/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock',\n                    '.../destination/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock',\n                    \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../source/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock'\")]\n\n## Mechanism (CONFIRMED by measurement, not inferred)\n\nThe test creates a bare `source/origin.git` with a raw `git init --bare`, pushes into it, and on the VERY NEXT statement runs `shutil.copytree(source_origin, destination_origin, symlinks=True)`.\n\nAt git's defaults a bare repository's `receive-pack` runs `run_auto_maintenance()` after every push, which spawns `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` — a background process that OUTLIVES the push. So `subprocess.run([... \"push\" ...], check=True)` returning is NOT a happens-before edge for that repository's object database. The copytree then walks a directory tree that a detached git process is concurrently rewriting.\n\nMeasured on this exact test with `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT`:\n\n- 3 `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` children (the repos the TEST creates itself)\n- 11 `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --no-detach` children (rebar-OWNED trackers, already pinned foreground by `_commands/init.py`'s gc-config ensure unit — bug 88eb, ADR 0051)\n\nA bare remote built by a test fixture is owned by no rebar code, so it runs at git's defaults. That is the entire gap.\n\n## The mechanism is BROADER than the observed signature\n\nA standalone deterministic reproduction (bare repo + push, `transfer.unpackLimit` raised so receive-pack explodes the push into loose objects, `gc.auto=1` so auto-maintenance has real work, then copytree immediately after the push returns) fails like this:\n\n    post-push maintenance.lock observed: True\n    copytree failure: shutil.Error: [('.../origin.git/objects/2c', ...,\n      \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../origin.git/objects/2c'\"),\n     ('.../origin.git/objects/2d', ...), ...]\n\nThe entries that vanish mid-walk are whole loose-object FANOUT DIRECTORIES being pruned as maintenance packs them. `objects/maintenance.lock` is merely the entry CI's walk happened to reach first.\n\nConsequence for the fix: filtering `*.lock` out of the copy would NOT de-flake this test. The repack limb remains wide open. The same second limb was measured on bug chewed-illicit-blacklemur, where ignoring `*.lock` was likewise shown insufficient.\n\n## Approach — remove the mutator, do not narrow the window\n\nPin the fixture bare remote's upkeep posture immediately after `git init --bare`, before anything is pushed into it:\n\n- `receive.autogc=false` — the direct fix. A throwaway fixture remote has no reason to run upkeep at all; measured, this drops the push's maintenance children to ZERO.\n- `gc.autoDetach=false` and `maintenance.autoDetach=false` — defence in depth for any other trigger. These do not suppress maintenance, they force it into the FOREGROUND, so the git command that triggered it cannot return while it is still running.\n\nEither way no mutator survives the push. Measured postures, all with `receive-pack` confirmed present in the trace:\n\n| posture | maintenance children | detached? |\n|---|---|---|\n| git defaults | 1 | yes — background mutator |\n| autoDetach pins only | 1 | no — foreground, push waits |\n| all three pins | 0 | n/a — no upkeep at all |\n\nThis is the same three-key remedy `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py` already applies to its own fixture remote (`_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS`, bug 5b74-5d8f-a6b4-4674). Explicitly NOT doing any of: retrying the copytree, sleeping before it, excluding `*.lock` from the copy, or relaxing any assertion. Each of those makes the flake rarer without making the test correct, and a rarer flake is worse — harder to diagnose, and it trains people to retry instead of investigate.\n\n## Guarding the fix against silent regression\n\nAsserting that the copy \"works\" cannot prove the mutator is gone — the race is a coin flip, so a green copy is consistent with the mutator still existing. So a new sibling test asserts the mutator's ABSENCE directly from git's own process trace: the push runs under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT`, and no `git maintenance run` child it spawns may carry `--detach`. A positive control first asserts the trace actually recorded the push's `receive-pack` child, so the guard cannot pass against an empty or unwritten trace. The assertion is a content fact about an argv list — no timing bound, no polling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py\n\nThe same \"raw `git init --bare` fixture remote at git defaults\" pattern exists elsewhere in the suite. A survey found two further HIGH-risk sites (a bare remote pushed into and then copied by `clone_topology_template`). Per scope discipline those are filed as a separate ticket with the evidence rather than absorbed into this change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The fixture bare remote in this test is created with `receive.autogc=false`, `gc.autoDetach=false` and `maintenance.autoDetach=false` pinned before anything is pushed into it; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] A push into that remote leaves no detached background upkeep running; checked by a new test that runs the push under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` and asserts no `git maintenance run` child carries `--detach`, with a `receive-pack` positive control so it cannot pass vacuously.\n- [ ] That new guard genuinely discriminates; checked by removing the pins and observing it go RED with the detached child in the failure message, then restoring them and observing GREEN.\n- [ ] The existing test still proves what it guards; checked by seeding a defect that stops the copy being re-pointed at its own sibling origin, observing RED on the test's own assertion, reverting, and observing GREEN.\n- [ ] The fix removes the race rather than tolerating it; checked by review of the diff for the absence of any retry loop, sleep, timing bound, or `*.lock` ignore predicate.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py -q` is green; checked by that command.\n- [ ] The whole `tests/interfaces` tier is green; checked by `pytest tests/interfaces -q`.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (requiring `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`) all pass; checked by running each."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787206990509901001,"uuid":"4896e13d-c9af-45ed-9099-47303f9da2c7"}